  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between NRF2 activator Geopyxin F and the CD276 antigen, as it is implicated in the activation of multiple targets that ultimately lead to the CD276 antigen. Specifically, Geopyxin F acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by Dendocarbin K and Bungeiside A. These compounds are all capable of interacting with the CD276 antigen, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that may involve the NRF2 signaling pathway. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Geopyxin F influences the CD276 antigen remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Geopyxin F in the regulation of CD276 antigen expression.",
